      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be good to avoid the `unwrap`s here because they provide a possibility of runtime error cases where we would ideally enforce everything at compile-time. The original `finish` method takes `self` by value, so there would be no need for the field to be an `Option`.\n\nDoes it work if you provide this method signature instead?\n\n```\n  pub fn finish(self: Box\u003cStreamWriter) -\u003e ffi::EncodingResult\n```\n\nI think it might!\n\nIf not perhaps you could switch this `finish` method from being a method into being a free function:\n\n```\npub fn finish_encode(this: Box\u003cStreamWriter) -\u003e ffi::EncodingResult\n```\n\nThat\u0027s not as neat and tidy but I personally would choose to value removal of runtime error paths over neatness. Up to you though.",
      "revId": "58cee891c9fff99cec1fdb3d2e1cc86b14a37bcd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
